# Landing / marketing page (`/`)

Read **`docs/NORTHSTAR.md`**, **`docs/LANDING.md`**, and **`docs/NAVIGATION.md` § Home** before changing Home, hero, or `homeMarketing.ts`.

## Voice (north star)

Lead with **find your people · get outside · go together** — not map/host architecture.

- **Audience:** residents, expats, tourists, visitors (UAE & GCC)  
- **Activities:** hikes, camps, runs, jogs, group outings — wide, with examples  
- **Mechanisms** (verified hosts, map, join flow) are supporting copy only  

## Audience (hard rule)

- **`/` is for signed-out guests only.**
- **Signed-in users always redirect to `/explore`** — they never see the marketing page.
- **`/explore` is the product home** (map-first discovery). Do not treat `/` as a second home or onboarding hub for members.

Enforced in `src/pages/Home.tsx`. Do not remove or bypass that redirect.

## What Home is

Guest **signup funnel**: emotional promise + trust + live proof → **Explore the map** / **Join free**. One pass, then the user lives on the map.

## What Home is not

Do **not** add to Home (unless the user explicitly asks):

- Demand / “find a group” flows, become-host, shops, buddies, chat, rewards 
- Full product tour or in-app feature documentation 
- Live map UX (filters, panels, pins) — that is `/explore` 

Home may mention *host-approved joins* and *real outings on the map* as trust/support — not as the lead headline.

